# What never enters the build context.
#
# Two reasons to keep this tight: a smaller context is a faster build, and
# anything that is not sent cannot end up in a layer by accident. Local secret
# material and environment files are excluded first, before convenience.
#
# Patterns are anchored at the context root unless they start with `**/`. A
# bare `.env` or `__pycache__` therefore matches only the one at the top level
# and misses every nested copy, which is the opposite of what both are for.
# Anything that can appear at any depth is written with `**/`.

# --- Local secret material and environment (never build with it) ---
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore
**/*.crt
**/*.cer
**/*.der
**/*.kubeconfig
**/kubeconfig
**/*-credentials.json
**/*_credentials.json
**/credentials.json
**/service-account*.json
**/sa-*.json
**/*.tfvars
**/*.unseal
**/unseal-keys*
**/root-token*
**/vault-token*
**/bao-token*
**/.bao-token
**/.vault-token

# --- Version control and CI ---
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# --- Build outputs and caches (the image builds its own) ---
**/node_modules
ui/dist
dist
build
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/*.egg-info

# --- Not part of the runtime ---
tests
terraform
deploy
docs
.agents
.claude
.editorconfig
.python-version
**/*.md

# --- Editors and OS ---
**/.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
